<title>UK: INSIGHT - Copper targets $2,300, aluminium firm.</title>
<headline>INSIGHT - Copper targets $2,300, aluminium firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> 3 MONTH     CLOSE  * SUPPORT * RESIST * RSI14 * MA10 * MA30</p>
<p> COPPER     2321/26 *  2240   *  2340  *  40   * 2292 * 2395</p>
<p> ALUMINIUM  1662/65 *  1600   *  1680  *  68   * 1600 * 1590</p>
<p>---------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - July 25----------------</p>
<p>Copper's ability to claw back above $2,300 a tonne despite rising stocks and a recent narrowing in nearby spreads suggests the market may be due for a short-covering bounce towards $2,350, traders and chartists said.</p>
<p>Aluminium looks set to extend this week's gains and is targeting $1,680 resistance against the backdrop of uptrending charts, they added.</p>
</text>
